<p class="xelementtoproof1" style="background:white"><span class="xelementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424;background:white">Good morning,&nbsp;</span></span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"></span></p>

<p class="xelementtoproof1" style="background:white"><span style="font-size:11.5pt;
color:#242424">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="xelementtoproof1" style="background:white"><span class="xelementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424;background:white">This week's discussion point was related
to the Russian/Ukraine conflict.&nbsp;</span></span><span style="color:#242424">&nbsp;Russian
media reported on 23 August that Wagner Group head Yevgeny&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"><a href="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/openremote/wfpub_eurasia_16188_189c9556/wfpub_eurasia_16188_189c9556.html" target="_blank" title="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/openremote/wfpub_eurasia_16188_189c9556/wfpub_eurasia_16188_189c9556.html"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">Prigozhin</span></a></span><span style="color:#242424">&nbsp;was
killed in a plane crash, flying between Moscow and St. Petersburg, with
possibly other senior Wagner personnel on board.&nbsp;The explanation of
Prigozhin’s death as a targeted killing is highly plausible, especially with
Wagner-affiliated social media channels and unverified videos claiming that the
Russian air defense shot the plane down. As for battlefield implications,
second large-scale revolt in reaction to Prigozhin’s death is unlikely, despite
angry messages coming from Wagner-aligned channels on social media. Prigozhin’s
death does not have significant reactions for Russian military operations in
Ukraine, since Wagner is not involved in Russia’s defensive operations in
Ukraine's south or offensive actions in Luhansk region in the east.</span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"></span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span style="color:#424242">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"></span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span class="xxxcontentpasted01"><span style="color:#242424;background:white">Picking up from last week when we
discussed China, Eurasia Group is downgrading its expectations for&nbsp;</span></span><span class="xxxcontentpasted01"><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424;
background:white"><a href="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16153_5644e92c/wfpub_eurasia_16153_5644e92c.html" target="_blank" title="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16153_5644e92c/wfpub_eurasia_16153_5644e92c.html"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">Chinese</span></a></span><span style="color:#242424;
background:white">&nbsp;growth this year to 4%-4.5% due to sustained demand
weakness, restrained stimulus, and the piecemeal nature of policy support; the
weakness in Chinese industry has become visible in the oil sector, and, if it
persists, could spill into 2024 and put pressure on OPEC+ to continue to
tightly manage supply.&nbsp;Growth will likely decelerate sequentially over the
next two quarters, given the&nbsp;steepening decline in the contribution of
real estate to GDP through investment and indirectly through consumption; a relatively
stable positive contribution from consumer services, which has outpaced slowing
spending on consumer goods; and a drag on growth from net exports as US and
European demand cools under sticky inflation and elevated rates.</span></span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"></span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span style="color:#424242">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"></span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span style="color:#242424">In<span class="xxxcontentpasted01">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;
color:#242424"><a href="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16149_70765666/wfpub_eurasia_16149_70765666.html" target="_blank" title="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16149_70765666/wfpub_eurasia_16149_70765666.html"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">Ecuador</span></a></span><span style="color:#242424">,
as we expected, correista candidate Luisa Gonzalez captured the most votes in
the 20 August first-round presidential election, with 33.4% (the same as in
2021); however, in a surprise, right-wing populist Daniel Noboa secured 24% of
the votes. They will face each other in the October 15<span class="xxxcontentpasted01"><sup>th</sup>&nbsp;runoff. Eurasia Group's basecase is
that Noboa is the initial favorite to win (a 60% probability).</span></span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"></span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span style="color:#424242">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"></span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span class="xxxcontentpasted01"><span style="color:#242424;background:white">Have a good weekend</span></span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"></span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span class="xxxcontentpasted01"><span style="color:#242424;background:white">Dave</span></span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;color:#242424"></span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span style="font-size:11.5pt;font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif;
color:#242424">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span class="xcontentpasted0"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif;color:black;background:
white">Eurasia Group Calls</span></b></span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;
font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif;color:#242424"></span></p>

<ul style="margin-top:0in" type="disc"><li class="xxxmsonormal" style="color:#424242;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list .5in;background:white"><span class="xcontentpasted0"><b><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:black;background:
     white">European natural gas, 2023-24 winter:</span></b></span><span class="xcontentpasted0"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;
     color:black;background:white">&nbsp;EU comes out of the upcoming winter
     with relatively high inventories,&nbsp;market conditions return to normal
     in 2024&nbsp;(50%); odds of&nbsp;EU gas inventories ending during the
     winter at very low levels, delaying a return to normal market conditions
     to 2025 or later&nbsp;(40%);&nbsp;odds of gas shortages in the EU (10%).
     Read&nbsp;</span></span><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;
     color:#0563C1;background:yellow"><a href="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16145_a189363e/wfpub_eurasia_16145_a189363e.html" target="_blank" title="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16145_a189363e/wfpub_eurasia_16145_a189363e.html"><span style="background:white">here</span></a></span><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:
     &quot;Times New Roman&quot;"></span></li><li class="xxxmsonormal" style="color:#424242;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list .5in;background:white"><span class="xcontentpasted0"><b><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:black;background:
     white">Ecuador&nbsp;presidential elections:</span></b></span><span class="xcontentpasted0"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;
     color:black;background:white">&nbsp;odds of Noboa to win (60%). Read&nbsp;</span></span><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:#0563C1;background:
     yellow"><a href="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16149_70765666/wfpub_eurasia_16149_70765666.html" target="_blank" title="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16149_70765666/wfpub_eurasia_16149_70765666.html"><span style="background:white">here</span></a></span><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:
     &quot;Times New Roman&quot;"></span></li><li class="xxxmsonormal" style="color:#424242;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list .5in;background:white"><span class="xcontentpasted0"><b><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:black;background:
     white">Japan lower house snap elections:</span></b></span><span class="xcontentpasted0"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;
     color:black;background:white">&nbsp;odds of Kishida calling the election
     before&nbsp;the end of the year (65%); odds of&nbsp;deferring the decision
     until 2024 (35%). Read&nbsp;<a href="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16185_2287ead1/wfpub_eurasia_16185_2287ead1.html" target="_blank" title="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16185_2287ead1/wfpub_eurasia_16185_2287ead1.html">here</a></span></span><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;"></span></li><li class="xxxmsonormal" style="color:#424242;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;
     tab-stops:list .5in;background:white"><span class="xcontentpasted0"><b><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:black;background:
     white">Iran nuclear program:</span></b></span><span class="xcontentpasted0"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;color:black;background:
     white">&nbsp;odds that US and Iran&nbsp;will continue to avoid
     escalation&nbsp;(65%, up from 60%); odds of a serious escalation (20%);
     an&nbsp;agreement combining concessions on enrichment with sanctions
     relief (10%); odds of&nbsp;returning to the 2015 nuclear deal&nbsp;(5%).
     Read&nbsp;</span></span><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;
     color:#0563C1;background:yellow"><a href="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16169_d58d306a/wfpub_eurasia_16169_d58d306a.html" target="_blank" title="https://library.eurasiagroup.net/document/view/wfpub_eurasia_16169_d58d306a/wfpub_eurasia_16169_d58d306a.html"><span style="background:white">here</span></a></span><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:
     &quot;Times New Roman&quot;"></span></li></ul>

<p class="xxxmsonormal" style="margin-left:.5in;background:white"><span class="xcontentpasted0"><span style="color:#424242">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="color:#242424"></span></p>

<p style="background:white"><span class="xcontentpasted0"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif;color:black;background:
white">Upcoming Events</span></b></span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;
font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif;color:#424242"><br>
</span><span class="xcontentpasted0"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif;color:black;background:white">Conference Calls</span></b></span><span style="font-size:11.5pt;font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif;color:#242424"></span></p>

<ul style="margin-top:0in" type="disc"><li class="xxxmsonormal" style="color:#424242;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;
